{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Image Generation \u2014 Diffusion Models Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: Noise schedule"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def linear_beta_schedule(T=1000, beta_start=1e-4, beta_end=2e-2):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return torch.linspace(beta_start, beta_end, T)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def precompute_schedule(betas):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    alphas = 1.0 - betas"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    alphas_cumprod = torch.cumprod(alphas, dim=0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return {"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"betas\": betas,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"alphas\": alphas,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"alphas_cumprod\": alphas_cumprod,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"sqrt_alphas_cumprod\": torch.sqrt(alphas_cumprod),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"sqrt_one_minus_alphas_cumprod\": torch.sqrt(1.0 - alphas_cumprod),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"sqrt_recip_alphas\": torch.sqrt(1.0 / alphas),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    }"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "schedule = precompute_schedule(linear_beta_schedule(T=1000))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Precompute once, gather by index during training and sampling."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Forward diffusion (q_sample)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def q_sample(x0, t, noise, schedule):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    sqrt_a = schedule[\"sqrt_alphas_cumprod\"][t].view(-1, 1, 1, 1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    sqrt_one_minus_a = schedule[\"sqrt_one_minus_alphas_cumprod\"][t].view(-1, 1, 1, 1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return sqrt_a * x0 + sqrt_one_minus_a * noise"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "One-line closed form. `t` is a batch of timesteps, one per image in the batch."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: A tiny time-conditioned U-Net"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch.nn as nn"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch.nn.functional as F"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import math"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def timestep_embedding(t, dim=64):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    half = dim // 2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    freqs = torch.exp(-math.log(10000) * torch.arange(half, device=t.device) / half)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    args = t[:, None].float() * freqs[None]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    emb = torch.cat([args.sin(), args.cos()], dim=-1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return emb"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class TinyUNet(nn.Module):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, img_channels=3, base=32, t_dim=64):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        super().__init__()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.t_mlp = nn.Sequential("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Linear(t_dim, base * 4),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.SiLU(),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Linear(base * 4, base * 4),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.t_dim = t_dim"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.enc1 = nn.Conv2d(img_channels, base, 3, padding=1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.enc2 = nn.Conv2d(base, base * 2, 4, stride=2, padding=1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.mid = nn.Conv2d(base * 2, base * 2, 3, padding=1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.dec1 = nn.ConvTranspose2d(base * 2, base, 4, stride=2, padding=1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.dec2 = nn.Conv2d(base * 2, img_channels, 3, padding=1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.time_proj = nn.Linear(base * 4, base * 2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, x, t):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        t_emb = timestep_embedding(t, self.t_dim)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        t_emb = self.t_mlp(t_emb)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        t_proj = self.time_proj(t_emb)[:, :, None, None]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        h1 = F.silu(self.enc1(x))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        h2 = F.silu(self.enc2(h1)) + t_proj"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        h3 = F.silu(self.mid(h2))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        d1 = F.silu(self.dec1(h3))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        d2 = torch.cat([d1, h1], dim=1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return self.dec2(d2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Two-level U-Net with time conditioning injected at the bottleneck. Scale up the depth and width for real images."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: Training loop"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def train_step(model, x0, schedule, optimizer, device, T=1000):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    model.train()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x0 = x0.to(device)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    bs = x0.size(0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    t = torch.randint(0, T, (bs,), device=device)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    noise = torch.randn_like(x0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x_t = q_sample(x0, t, noise, schedule)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    pred = model(x_t, t)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    loss = F.mse_loss(pred, noise)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    optimizer.zero_grad()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    loss.backward()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    optimizer.step()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return loss.item()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "That is the entire training loop. No GAN game, no specialised loss, one MSE call."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: Sampler (DDPM)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "@torch.no_grad()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def sample(model, schedule, shape, T=1000, device=\"cpu\"):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    model.eval()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x = torch.randn(shape, device=device)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    betas = schedule[\"betas\"].to(device)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    sqrt_one_minus_a = schedule[\"sqrt_one_minus_alphas_cumprod\"].to(device)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    sqrt_recip_alphas = schedule[\"sqrt_recip_alphas\"].to(device)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for t in reversed(range(T)):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        t_batch = torch.full((shape[0],), t, dtype=torch.long, device=device)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        eps = model(x, t_batch)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        coef = betas[t] / sqrt_one_minus_a[t]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        mean = sqrt_recip_alphas[t] * (x - coef * eps)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if t > 0:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            x = mean + torch.sqrt(betas[t]) * torch.randn_like(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        else:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            x = mean"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return x"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "1000 forward passes to produce one batch of samples. In real code you would swap this for a DDIM 50-step sampler."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 6: DDIM sampler (deterministic, ~20x faster)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "@torch.no_grad()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def sample_ddim(model, schedule, shape, steps=50, T=1000, device=\"cpu\", eta=0.0):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    model.eval()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x = torch.randn(shape, device=device)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    alphas_cumprod = schedule[\"alphas_cumprod\"].to(device)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ts = torch.linspace(T - 1, 0, steps + 1).long()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for i in range(steps):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        t = ts[i]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        t_prev = ts[i + 1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        t_batch = torch.full((shape[0],), t, dtype=torch.long, device=device)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        eps = model(x, t_batch)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        a_t = alphas_cumprod[t]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        a_prev = alphas_cumprod[t_prev] if t_prev >= 0 else torch.tensor(1.0, device=device)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x0_pred = (x - torch.sqrt(1 - a_t) * eps) / torch.sqrt(a_t)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        sigma = eta * torch.sqrt((1 - a_prev) / (1 - a_t) * (1 - a_t / a_prev))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        dir_xt = torch.sqrt(1 - a_prev - sigma ** 2) * eps"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        noise = sigma * torch.randn_like(x) if eta > 0 else 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = torch.sqrt(a_prev) * x0_pred + dir_xt + noise"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return x"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`eta=0` is fully deterministic (same noise input always produces the same output). `eta=1` recovers DDPM."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **(Easy)** Visualise the forward process: take one image and plot `x_t` at `t in [0, 100, 250, 500, 750, 1000]`. Verify that `x_1000` looks like pure Gaussian noise.\n2. **(Medium)** Train the TinyUNet on the synthetic-circles dataset for 20 epochs and sample 16 circles. Compare DDPM (1000 steps) and DDIM (50 steps) sampling \u2014 do they produce similar images from the same noise seed?\n3. **(Hard)** Implement a cosine noise schedule (Nichol & Dhariwal, 2021): `alpha_bar_t = cos^2((t/T + s) / (1 + s) * pi / 2)`. Train the same model with linear and cosine schedules and show that cosine gives better samples at low step counts."
      ]
    }
